0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$ where ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-332596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{5t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])"] ["math" "{e}^{5t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}(t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]){e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$ where ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-332595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])"] ["math" "{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+2t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$ where ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+2t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is a polynomial in $t$ of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $2$, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-332805" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332805" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{-t}(t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}])"] ["math" "{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332805" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution has the same exponential factor, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-332739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}])"] ["math" "{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}(t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]){e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-332749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{-t}(t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}])"] ["math" "{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} \\\\ -2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} \\\\ -2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0t+{a}_{1} \\\\ 0t+{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}({a}_{2}-2)t+({b}_{2}+1) \\\\ (-2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+8)t+(-2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2})\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2}-2=0 \\\\ -2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+8=0 \\\\ {b}_{2}+1={a}_{1} \\\\ -2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2}={a}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first two equations, we get \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2,\\,{a}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting these into the third and fourth equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=0,\\,{b}_{1}=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-333007" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333007" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333007" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333007" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-3t+4 \\\\ 2t-1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | $\\frac{11}{6}$ |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3t+4 \\\\ 2t-1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined.\n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-3t+4 \\\\ 2t-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ 3{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ 3{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t+4 \\\\ 2t-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0t+{a}_{1} \\\\ 0t+{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-3)t+(2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}+4) \\\\ (3{a}_{2}+2)t+(3{b}_{2}-1)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-3=0 \\\\ 3{a}_{2}+2=0 \\\\ 2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}+4={a}_{1} \\\\ 3{b}_{2}-1={a}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe first two equations, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3},\\,{a}_{1}=\\frac{11}{6}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the third and fourth equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{9},\\,{b}_{1}=-\\frac{41}{36}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{41}{36} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-333008" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333008" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{41}{36}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333008" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333008" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}t-3 \\\\ 2t+1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | $-\\frac{7}{4}$ |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $\\frac{3}{8}$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}t-3 \\\\ 2t+1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1/2 & 3/2 \\\\ 3/2 & -1/2\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}t-3 \\\\ 2t+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}({a}_{1}t+{b}_{1})+\\frac{3}{2}({a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}({a}_{1}t+{b}_{1})-\\frac{1}{2}({a}_{2}t+{b}_{2})\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t-3 \\\\ 2t+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0t+{a}_{1} \\\\ 0t+{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{{a}_{1}}{2}+\\frac{3{a}_{2}}{2}+1)t+(-\\frac{{b}_{1}}{2}+\\frac{3{b}_{2}}{2}-3) \\\\ (\\frac{3{a}_{1}}{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}}{2}+2)t+(\\frac{3{b}_{1}}{2}-\\frac{{b}_{2}}{2}+1)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{a}_{1}}{2}+\\frac{3{a}_{2}}{2}+1=0 \\\\ \\frac{3{a}_{1}}{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}}{2}+2=0 \\\\ -\\frac{{b}_{1}}{2}+\\frac{3{b}_{2}}{2}-3={a}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{3{b}_{1}}{2}-\\frac{{b}_{2}}{2}+1={a}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first two equations, we get \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=-\\frac{7}{4},\\,{a}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting these into the third and fourth equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=-\\frac{11}{8},\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{8} \\\\ \\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-333010" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333010" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{11}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333010" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333010" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{5}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\cdot \\,\\,$ |  | $2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=-4{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -4[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-4a \\\\ -4b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a \\\\ 5b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-4a \\\\ -4b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a-14 \\\\ 5b-27\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3a-14=-4a \\\\ 5b-27=-4b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n3a-14=-4a\\,⇒\\,a=2.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n5b-27=-4b\\,⇒\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-332914" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332914" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{-4t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332914" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332914" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+$ {{field-1}} $\\cdot \\,\\,$ |  | $-\\frac{7}{10}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=-{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-a \\\\ -b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3b \\\\ 3a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-a \\\\ -b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3b+4 \\\\ 3a+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3b+4=-a \\\\ 3a+1=-b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\na=3b-4.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n3(3b-4)+1=-b\\,⇒\\,b=\\frac{11}{10}.\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\na=3\\cdot \\frac{11}{10}-4=\\frac{33}{10}-\\frac{40}{10}=-\\frac{7}{10}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{10} \\\\ \\frac{11}{10}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-332866" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-332866" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{-t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4