$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(0)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{3(0)}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-(0)^{2}+2 \\\\ (0)^{2}-0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2 \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2=8 \\\\ {c}_{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=6.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-7.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-7\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38be8d6943407c7a7c2b31cb"} {"question" "q-333611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad2a51c3104c829087039fd85ba5dc7fe4c610f46a2a25976081cfaa2a1446bb"} {"question" "q-333611" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea