 nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-1 \\\\ -2t+3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-1 \\\\ -2\\cdot 0+3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-1 \\\\ {c}_{2}+3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-1=10 \\\\ {c}_{2}+3=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=11.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=9.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=11\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-1 \\\\ -2t+3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/state.json" "file_sha256" "d822f5cea8e8fa86991ed476fcb4167e10bee94e38b